# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Apify credentials (SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never expose to the client)
#
# 1. Create an account at https://apify.com
# 2. Go to Settings → Integrations → API token and copy your token.
# 3. Paste the token below (or into .env.local, which is gitignored).
#
# NOTE: Do NOT rename these to NEXT_PUBLIC_* — doing so would leak
# the token into the browser bundle.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APIFY_API_TOKEN=

# The Apify Actor used to scrape public Instagram post data.
# Default used by the app when this is empty: apify/instagram-scraper
# Any Actor that accepts a list of Instagram post URLs and returns
# dataset items with image/media URLs will work — see lib/apify.ts
# for the documented input/output contract.
APIFY_ACTOR_ID=
